WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Football has more to say than the score. This is Agora Match.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:10.144
One synthetic match becomes three distinct experiences. Fans follow the story. Analysts

00:00:10.144 --> 00:00:13.031
inspect evidence. Coaches prepare focused reviews.

00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:19.432
Play the match, follow the ball, and jump straight to key moments. The replay uses

00:00:19.432 --> 00:00:21.383
fictional events and illustrative tracking.

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:26.958
At a corner, Agora connects the current moment with both teams' recent set piece

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:30.188
history. Every claim keeps its sample size and source.

00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:35.504
Ask the match in plain language. Open the supporting facts, then follow an event link

00:00:35.504 --> 00:00:36.775
back to the pitch.

00:00:37.325 --> 00:00:42.828
Analysts can find tagged winger versus fullback encounters, and inspect each outcome

00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:44.663
alongside prior player positions.

00:00:45.213 --> 00:00:50.160
Rewind to twenty minutes. Later evidence disappears. The score becomes nil nil, and

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.063
eight tagged encounters become one.

00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:57.181
Follow any player for position specific metrics, a movement heatmap, historical

00:00:57.181 --> 00:00:59.672
context, and a transparent demo rating.

00:01:00.222 --> 00:01:05.908
Coaches get qualified review cues. Lower sampled running output and wider spacing

00:01:05.908 --> 00:01:10.172
trigger questions, not fatigue diagnoses or assumed marking errors.

00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:16.313
Package a finding as a timed broadcast card, with machine readable evidence and an

00:01:16.313 --> 00:01:16.713
expiry.

00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:22.407
An optional Microsoft Foundry workflow separates analysis, audience narration, and

00:01:22.407 --> 00:01:28.580
review. Code preserves fact values. This public demo uses deterministic answers. Live

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.638
model evaluation remains pending.

00:01:31.188 --> 00:01:36.308
Explore two fictional matches. Ask, inspect, and share the story behind the score.
